# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Data Science with R (AECN 896-05)
#
# Two things this file must NOT break:
#   1. docs/ is the published site. GitHub Pages serves it. It is TRACKED,
#      including its *_files/ asset directories.
#   2. lectures/Chapter-9-Spatial-Data/Data/PRISM/ is read at render time and
#      its contents are PRINTED on a slide. Every sidecar there is tracked,
#      including .prj and .xml. See "Chapter 9 data" below.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Quarto / knitr intermediates ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Scoped to the source tree so docs/**/*_files/ survives. /.quarto/ also holds
# a live deno-kv database that Dropbox creates conflicted copies of.
/.quarto/
/*_files/
/*_cache/
/lectures/**/*_files/
/lectures/**/*_cache/
/exercises/**/*_files/
/exercises/**/*_cache/
/syllabus/**/*_files/
/syllabus/**/*_cache/
/templates/**/*_files/
/templates/**/*_cache/

# ── Student work: never in a public repository ───────────────────────────────
# 825 MB, and *_submission/ holds identifiable student work (FERPA).
# Assignments are distributed to students by Dropbox link, not from this repo,
# so nothing here is published. The old rule said "Assignments/" (capital A)
# and did not match the directory, which is actually named "assignments/".
/assignments/

# Student names and @huskers.unl.edu addresses.
/roster/

# ── Directories that are separate git repositories ───────────────────────────
# Tracking these would create broken gitlinks in the new repo.
/sample-project-reproducible/
/supplementary-material/
/data/

# ── Not part of the course site ──────────────────────────────────────────────
/sample-project/
/templates/
/Video/
/Datasets/
/FinalProject/
# Contains a business proposal, not course material.
# BOTH rules are needed. _quarto.yml does not exclude this from the render, so
# a full render keeps regenerating docs/IndustryPartnership/. Ignoring only the
# source would still publish the rendered proposal, because GitHub Pages serves
# whatever is committed under docs/.
/IndustryPartnership/
/docs/IndustryPartnership/

# ── Chapter 9 data ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# TRACKED (required to render; do not add extension globs that catch these):
#   Data/PRISM/**            9 .bil rasters + .hdr/.prj/.xml/.stx sidecars.
#                            Two live chunks list this folder and print the
#                            result, so its contents are visible output.
#                            .prj carries the CRS - drop it and the printed
#                            SpatRaster loses "coord. ref. : lon/lat NAD83".
#   Data/il_ne_corn_yield.rds   read by an include=FALSE chunk.
#
# IGNORED below: master copies of the student Dropbox bundle. Every chunk that
# names them is eval=FALSE and points at "data-files-for-participants/", a
# folder that does not exist here. They are never read by the render.
/lectures/Chapter-9-Spatial-Data/Data/gm_precip_2018.nc
/lectures/Chapter-9-Spatial-Data/Data/gm_precip_2018.nc.aux.*
/lectures/Chapter-9-Spatial-Data/Data/reflec_*.tif
/lectures/Chapter-9-Spatial-Data/Data/nc_practice.*
/lectures/Chapter-9-Spatial-Data/Data/blue.rds
# Note the path: this one is directly under Data/, NOT under Data/PRISM/.
/lectures/Chapter-9-Spatial-Data/Data/PRISM_ppt_stable_4kmD2_20120801_bil/

# ── Credentials ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# L06 once carried a live USDA-NASS key that reached the public site.
.Renviron
.env
*.pem

# ── LaTeX byproducts ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Scoped to the source tree: docs/ may legitimately serve a .pdf or .tex.
/lectures/**/*.tex
/lectures/**/*.aux
/lectures/**/*.log
/exercises/**/*.tex
/syllabus/**/*.tex

# ── R / RStudio ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.Rproj.user/
.Rhistory
.RData
.Ruserdata
*.Rproj

# ── Editor and OS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*~
.vscode/
# Machine-specific paths; the rest of .claude/ is shared and tracked.
.claude/settings.local.json

# ── Dropbox ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This repo lives in Dropbox, which leaves these behind after a sync race.
*conflicted copy*
.dropbox
.dropbox.attr

# ── Stray artefacts from running chunks interactively ────────────────────────
/a_list.rds
/_tmp-open.html

# ── Personal notes ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*/chatGPT_questions.md
